"Foo", one of "foo", "bar", "baz", is a term from
the Unix/c programming community for a "generic
something".

In the case of "foocubi", it means incubi OR succubi
(male demons of lust and female demons of lust,
respectively).

The "vanilla" or standard distribution of NetHack is
heterosexual, so same-gender foocubi will attack
you, opposite-gender foocubi will attack you or
attempt to seduce you, depending on their mood (and
perhaps your charisma, I don't know).

It turns out that consorting with foocubi "makes one
'more experienced'" in the sniggering high school
sense, which in NetHack translates to improved
experience levels, or XLs.

When one has been "consorting with foocubi" a lot,
ones XL is probably high. This is not an unmixed
blessing; it gives you lots of skill slots and hit
points, but it also means the game generates tougher
monsters to make sure you are still being
challenged.  Having a high XL and a poor armor class
is a good recipe for an early demise, as a result.

